    "title": "Mako, Culver to Bring Attention to Organ Donation",
    "url": "http://www.repmako.com/News/38856/Press-Releases/Mako--Culver-to-Bring-Attention-to-Organ-Donation",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Mako, Culver to Bring Attention to Organ Donation\nOctober 2, 2026\nWHAT:\nRep. Zach Mako (R-Lehigh/Northampton) and Sen. Lynda Schlegel Culver (R-27) will help bring attention to organ donation by leading the Steps for Life Advocacy Walk. It will begin with a brief press conference and then a short walk around the Capitol grounds.\nWHO:\nMako, Culver, and Gift of Life Donor Program leaders and a transplant recipient.\nWHEN:\nMonday, Oct. 5, 10 a.m.\nWHERE:\nMain Capitol Rotunda, Harrisburg\n.\nLIVE WEBSTREAMING:\nTune in at\nRepMako.com\n.\nMedia contact:\nTracy Polovick, 717.260.6358,\ntpolovick@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "State Representative Zach Mako and State Senator Lynda Schlegel Culver will participate in the Steps for Life Advocacy Walk on October 5, 2026, an event organized to raise awareness about organ donation. The event includes a press conference and a walk around the Capitol grounds, held in partnership with the Gift of Life Donor Program.",
      "action_type": "event",
      "topics": [
        "healthcare",
        "other"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Mako to Host Disability Resource Fair",
    "url": "http://www.repmako.com/News/38857/Press-Releases/Mako-to-Host-Disability-Resource-Fair",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Mako to Host Disability Resource Fair\nOctober 1, 2026\nHARRISBURG\n– In an effort to assist individuals with disabilities and their families, Rep. Zach Mako (R-Lehigh/Northampton) will soon host his third annual Disabilities Resource Fair.\nThe free event will be held on Saturday, Oct. 24, from 10 a.m. to noon, at Union Lutheran Church,\n5500 Route 873, Schnecksville\n.\n“This event has been a highlight of mine,” Mako said. “Empowering those with disabilities, their loved ones and caregivers with the resources to create opportunities to live life to the fullest should never be discounted. Whether you have attended in the past or this will be your first time, I look forward to seeing you.”\nAttendees will have the opportunity to visit with nearly 40 local, state and federal agencies and organizations offering information on programs and services available to both individuals with disabilities and caregivers.\nLight refreshments will be available, as well as live music courtesy of Hearts for Music, an organization that creates opportunities for individuals with disabilities to pursue their love of creating and performing music in an ensemble setting.\nThe 183rd District includes Lowhill and North Whitehall townships and Slatington Borough in Lehigh County. It also consists of Allen, East Allen, Lehigh and Moore (part) townships, and Bath, North Catasauqua, Northampton and Walnutport boroughs in Northampton County.\nRepresentative Zach Mako\n183rd Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tracy Polovick\n717.260.6358\ntpolovick@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Rep. Zach Mako is hosting a free Disabilities Resource Fair on October 24, 2026, from 10 a.m. to noon at Union Lutheran Church in Schnecksville. The event will bring together nearly 40 local, state, and federal agencies to provide information on programs and services for people with disabilities and their caregivers. This is the third year Mako has organized the event.",
      "action_type": "event",
      "topics": [
        "healthcare",
        "other"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
  },
  {
    "title": "Mako, Culver Spotlight Organ Donation",
    "url": "http://www.repmako.com/News/38863/Press-Releases/Mako--Culver-Spotlight-Organ-Donation",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Mako, Culver Spotlight Organ Donation\nOctober 5, 2026\nHARRISBURG – Rep. Zach Mako (R-Lehigh/Northampton) and Sen. Lynda Schlegel Culver (R-27) today joined the Gift of Life Donor Program, donor families and transplant recipients to raise awareness about organ donation and encourage Pennsylvanians to register as donors.\nThe two legislators, both organ donor recipients, spoke at a press conference in the Capitol Rotunda and then participated in the Steps for Life Advocacy Walk around the building.\n“I wouldn’t be standing here today without the gift I received, and without a family who, in the middle of their own grief, made the choice to give someone else a second chance,” Mako said. “That decision gave me my life back. I’m able to continue serving in the National Guard, travel and stay active in ways I never take for granted. Every year, this walk reminds me why we can’t let that momentum stop, and I want every Pennsylvanian on the waiting list to have the chance I had. That starts with more people registering as organ donors.”\n“Organ donation is deeply personal to me because a living donor saved my life,” Culver said. “I was fortunate to have someone in my own family who was a match and willing to make that sacrifice. That gift is why I am still here today, able to be with my family, serve my community and do the work I do. Today’s walk is an opportunity to recognize donors and donor families, support transplant recipients and remind people just how much one decision can change another person’s life.”\nAccording to the Gift of Life Donor Program, more than 6,000 Pennsylvanians are currently waiting for a lifesaving organ transplant. Participants also heard from a donor family and a transplant recipient about how organ donation changed their lives.\nInformation about organ donation and donor registration is available through the Gift of Life Donor Program at\ndonors1.org\n.\nThe 183rd District includes Lowhill and North Whitehall townships and Slatington Borough in Lehigh County. It also consists of Allen, East Allen, Lehigh and Moore (part) townships, and Bath, North Catasauqua, Northampton and Walnutport boroughs in Northampton County.\nRepresentative Zach Mako\n183rd Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tracy Polovick\n717.260.6358\ntpolovick@pahousegop.com\nRepMako.com / Facebook.com/RepMako\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Rep. Zach Mako and Sen. Lynda Schlegel Culver, both organ transplant recipients, appeared at a press conference in the Capitol Rotunda and participated in an advocacy walk to promote organ donor registration in Pennsylvania. The event was organized by the Gift of Life Donor Program and also featured a donor family and a transplant recipient. No legislation was introduced or advanced.",
      "action_type": "event",
      "topics": [
        "healthcare",
        "public_safety"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
  },
