  {
    "title": "Mako, Culver Spotlight Organ Donation",
    "url": "https://www.repmako.com/News/38863/Press-Releases/Mako--Culver-Spotlight-Organ-Donation",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Mako, Culver Spotlight Organ Donation\nOctober 5, 2026\nHARRISBURG – Rep. Zach Mako (R-Lehigh/Northampton) and Sen. Lynda Schlegel Culver (R-27) today joined the Gift of Life Donor Program, donor families and transplant recipients to raise awareness about organ donation and encourage Pennsylvanians to register as donors.\nThe two legislators, both organ donor recipients, spoke at a press conference in the Capitol Rotunda and then participated in the Steps for Life Advocacy Walk around the building.\n“I wouldn’t be standing here today without the gift I received, and without a family who, in the middle of their own grief, made the choice to give someone else a second chance,” Mako said. “That decision gave me my life back. I’m able to continue serving in the National Guard, travel and stay active in ways I never take for granted. Every year, this walk reminds me why we can’t let that momentum stop, and I want every Pennsylvanian on the waiting list to have the chance I had. That starts with more people registering as organ donors.”\n“Organ donation is deeply personal to me because a living donor saved my life,” Culver said. “I was fortunate to have someone in my own family who was a match and willing to make that sacrifice. That gift is why I am still here today, able to be with my family, serve my community and do the work I do. Today’s walk is an opportunity to recognize donors and donor families, support transplant recipients and remind people just how much one decision can change another person’s life.”\nAccording to the Gift of Life Donor Program, more than 6,000 Pennsylvanians are currently waiting for a lifesaving organ transplant. Participants also heard from a donor family and a transplant recipient about how organ donation changed their lives.\nInformation about organ donation and donor registration is available through the Gift of Life Donor Program at\ndonors1.org\n.\nThe 183rd District includes Lowhill and North Whitehall townships and Slatington Borough in Lehigh County. It also consists of Allen, East Allen, Lehigh and Moore (part) townships, and Bath, North Catasauqua, Northampton and Walnutport boroughs in Northampton County.\nRepresentative Zach Mako\n183rd Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tracy Polovick\n717.260.6358\ntpolovick@pahousegop.com\nRepMako.com / Facebook.com/RepMako\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "State Representative Zach Mako and State Senator Lynda Schlegel Culver, both organ transplant recipients, spoke at a Capitol press conference and participated in a walking event organized by the Gift of Life Donor Program to promote organ donor registration. No legislation was introduced or voted on. The event also featured remarks from a donor family and a transplant recipient.",
      "action_type": "event",
      "topics": [
        "healthcare",
        "public_safety"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
  },
