  {
    "title": "Mako to Host Disability Resource Fair",
    "url": "https://www.repmako.com/News/38857/Press-Releases/Mako-to-Host-Disability-Resource-Fair",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Mako to Host Disability Resource Fair\nOctober 1, 2026\nHARRISBURG\n– In an effort to assist individuals with disabilities and their families, Rep. Zach Mako (R-Lehigh/Northampton) will soon host his third annual Disabilities Resource Fair.\nThe free event will be held on Saturday, Oct. 24, from 10 a.m. to noon, at Union Lutheran Church,\n5500 Route 873, Schnecksville\n.\n“This event has been a highlight of mine,” Mako said. “Empowering those with disabilities, their loved ones and caregivers with the resources to create opportunities to live life to the fullest should never be discounted. Whether you have attended in the past or this will be your first time, I look forward to seeing you.”\nAttendees will have the opportunity to visit with nearly 40 local, state and federal agencies and organizations offering information on programs and services available to both individuals with disabilities and caregivers.\nLight refreshments will be available, as well as live music courtesy of Hearts for Music, an organization that creates opportunities for individuals with disabilities to pursue their love of creating and performing music in an ensemble setting.\nThe 183rd District includes Lowhill and North Whitehall townships and Slatington Borough in Lehigh County. It also consists of Allen, East Allen, Lehigh and Moore (part) townships, and Bath, North Catasauqua, Northampton and Walnutport boroughs in Northampton County.\nRepresentative Zach Mako\n183rd Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tracy Polovick\n717.260.6358\ntpolovick@pahousegop.com\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Rep. Zach Mako is hosting a free Disabilities Resource Fair on October 24, 2026, from 10 a.m. to noon at Union Lutheran Church in Schnecksville. The event will bring together nearly 40 local, state, and federal agencies to provide information on programs and services for people with disabilities and their caregivers. This is the third year Mako has organized the event.",
      "action_type": "event",
      "topics": [
        "healthcare",
        "other"
      ],
      "spin_flag": false
    }
