  {
    "title": "Municipalities in 183rd Awarded Grants, Mako Says",
    "url": "https://www.repmako.com/News/37992/Press-Releases/Municipalities-in-183rd-Awarded-Grants--Mako-Says",
    "date": null,
    "raw_text": "Municipalities in 183rd Awarded Grants, Mako Says\nMay 20, 2026\nHARRISBURG – Rep. Zach Mako (R-Lehigh/Northampton) today announced he helped secure almost $523,000 in Local Share Account (LSA) grants from the Commonwealth Financing Authority (CFA) for projects in the 183rd Legislative District.\nAct 71 of 2004 provides for the distribution of LSA gaming revenues through the CFA to support projects of public interest within the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania.\n“I’m grateful to partner with Sens. Nick Miller and Jarrett Coleman to secure funding for these projects,” Mako said. “These resources will support the repair and replacement of essential infrastructure and equipment that municipalities and organizations rely on to better serve our community. I’m glad to help pursue this funding, as moving forward without it would have been difficult.”\nMunicipalities receiving LSA funding are:\n•\tNorthampton Borough – $59,397 to replace the police chief’s command vehicle.\n•\tLehigh Township – $89,500 to replace its mobile vehicle radios in its police vehicles and its base station at the police department due to a change in Northampton County 911 dispatching.\n•\tLehigh Township – $60,987 to replace its police radios to secure, modern digital devices, which will improve interoperability with surrounding areas.\n•\tSlatington Borough – $36,241 to purchase a new patrol vehicle for the police department.\n•\tSlatington Borough – $17,422 to make critical roof repairs to the Slatington Public Library.\n•\tWalnutport Borough – $56,911 to purchase a new camera system for four patrol cars, body-worn cameras for its officers and tasers.\n•\tWalnutport Borough – $202,432 to replace an aging and malfunctioning municipal dump truck.\nThe 183rd House District includes Lowhill and North Whitehall townships and Slatington Borough in Lehigh County. It also consists of Allen, East Allen, Lehigh and Moore (part) townships, and Bath, North Catasauqua, Northampton and Walnutport boroughs in Northampton County.\nRepresentative Zachary Mako\n183rd Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tracy Polovick\n717.260.6358\ntpolovick@pahousegop.com\nRepMako.com / Facebook.com/RepMako\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "Several municipalities in Pennsylvania's 183rd Legislative District received a combined $522,890 in state gaming revenue grants through the Commonwealth Financing Authority. The funds will go toward public safety equipment and infrastructure projects, including police vehicles, radios, body cameras, tasers, a dump truck, and library roof repairs. Rep. Mako worked alongside two state senators to apply for and secure these grants.",
      "action_type": "other",
      "topics": [
        "public_safety",
        "infrastructure"
      ],
      "spin_flag": true
    }
