    "raw_text": "Low-Interest Loan Awarded for Slatington Water Project, Mako Says\nJuly 16, 2025\nHARRISBURG – Rep. Zach Mako (R-Lehigh/Northampton) today announced the Borough of Slatington has been awarded a $993,340 low-interest loan for a drinking water project.\nThe Pennsylvania Infrastructure Investment Authority (PENNVEST) funding will be used to purchase and install 1,409 water meters accompanied by an enhanced data collection system to streamline meter reading and billing operations.\n“By updating the meters, time spent gathering water usage for correct billing can be reduced,” Mako said. “This will modernize operations in order to allow for employees to work more efficiently.”\nPENNVEST funds sewer, storm water and drinking water projects throughout the Commonwealth through low-interest loans and grants.\nThe 183rd District includes Lowhill and North Whitehall townships and Slatington Borough in Lehigh County. It also consists of Allen, East Allen, Lehigh and Moore (part) townships, and Bath, North Catasauqua, Northampton and Walnutport boroughs in Northampton County.\nRepresentative Zachary Mako\n183rd Legislative District\nPennsylvania House of Representatives\nMedia Contact: Tracy Polovick\n717.260.6358\ntpolovick@pahousegop.com\nRepMako.com / Facebook.com/RepMako\nShare\nSign Up to Receive Legislative Email Updates\nKeep up-to-date on the latest legislative and community news. Your email address will be used strictly for legislative purposes.\nEmail*\nZIP Code\nSubscribe",
    "ai_summary": {
      "summary": "The Borough of Slatington, Pennsylvania has received a $993,340 low-interest loan from PENNVEST to replace 1,409 water meters and install a new data collection system. The funding will modernize how the borough tracks water usage and handles billing. Rep. Mako announced the award but did not directly secure the funding; PENNVEST is a state authority that funds water infrastructure projects across Pennsylvania.",
